    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This report covers the results from the fourth year of the Shale Smear Project. It includes the final results from the Gulf of Suez, Egypt and the Niger Delta. We have just initiated a new study in Black Diamond Mine Regional Park. A progress report from this study will be presented.\r\n\r\nTable of Contents:\r\n\"Progress Report on shale smear study at Black Diamond Mine, California.\" Atilla Aydin.\r\n\"3D Fault segmentation: implications for entrapment and compartmentalisation.\" Thierry Rives and Antonio Benedicto.\r\n\"Normal fault segmentation along dip direction and its impact on fault sealing.\" Poster 1. Amgad Younes and Atilla Aydin. \r\n\"A new, process-based methodology for the analysis of faults and their sealing potential in the Niger Delta.\" Poster 2. Bashir Koledoye, Atilla Aydin, and Eric May.\r\n\"Segmented faults: dynamic behavior in well test simulations.\" Poster 3. Eric Caput, Thierry Rives, and Yann Lagelaye.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
